Mix components and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere. After cooling, add the following solutions from sterile anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10% CaCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O solution                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 12.5% Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>&#183;5H<sub>2</sub>O solution*        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;20.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                     </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Adjust pH of the medium to 6.7 - 6.8, if necessary.       <br>
